\section{Experimental Setup and Metrics}\label{sec:method}

\subsection{Benchmark, Models, and Evaluation}\label{sec:benchmark}

We evaluate on SafeLIBERO~\cite{hu2025vlsa}, a collision-aware extension of LIBERO~\cite{liu2023libero} with per-timestep collision detection. We use the \textit{object\_pudding} suite (Level~I): four tabletop pick-and-place tasks where non-target objects create collision hazards. We evaluate two VLA families: \textbf{Pi0} (${\sim}$2.5B parameters)~\cite{black2024pi0}, which generates continuous actions via flow matching~\cite{lipman2023flow}, and \textbf{Pi0.5}, which extends Pi0 with broader pre-training and higher task capability. Table~\ref{tab:configurations} summarizes all seven configurations. Each is evaluated with 50 episodes per task (200 total); Pi0.5 multi-seed experiments use 3 seeds (600 episodes). We report Collision Avoidance Rate (CAR), the fraction of collision-free episodes, and Task Success Rate (TSR), the fraction of episodes achieving task completion~\cite{hu2025vlsa,zhang2025safevla}.

